   219	
   220	## Gate results
   221	
   222	### Gate A — PASS
   223	
   224	- A1: the exact program body executes under fixed semantics. The KORE identity
   225	  check ties the abbreviation to `solution.mpy`; a material body mutation is
   226	  rejected.
   227	- A2: no operational bridge skips state transitions. Claims constrain the
   228	  heap, environment, counters, stack, return state, exception state, and exit
   229	  code.
   230	- A3: fixed lookup, left-to-right argument evaluation, binding, branch
   231	  control, return, and frame-pop rules execute. No proof rule pins or bypasses
   232	  a binding or continuation.
   233	- A4: all proof-local equations are truthful on their constructor domains.
   234	  `expectedCompare` has disjoint, exhaustive Boolean guards. No false
   235	  simplification or global axiom was added.
   236	- A5: `(1, 2)` realizes the precondition. The false result claim is rejected
   237	  at result `2`, and every target result is constrained by
   238	  `expectedCompare`.
   239	
   240	### Gate B — PASS
   241	
   242	- B1: the nine claims cover every pairing of the three source-contract types
   243	  over unbounded modeled values. No size bound, finite enumeration, or
   244	  candidate-added domain restriction appears in the theorem.
   245	- B2: the theorem covers every value represented by the fixed model. The
   246	  supplied model's ASCII and decimal-parser limits, opaque symbolic IEEE
   247	  comparisons, and CPython edge differences are recorded below rather than
   248	  hidden as theorem restrictions.
   249	- B3: the formal theorem proves the exact execution/result relationship under
   250	  MPY. Its interpretation as ordering of real values is conditional on the
   251	  named supplied numeric primitives.
   252	- B4: the Python implementation matches the contract on real-number inputs.
   253	  It returns one of the original arguments and uses neither conversion result
   254	  as the returned object.
   255	
   256	### Gate C — PASS
   257	
   258	Every unproved primitive is listed in the trust ledger with its value/control
   259	influence and dependents. Every claimed concrete, differential, mutation, and
   260	model-boundary check has an artifact, command, actual exit status, and result.
   261	Finite evidence is reported only as evidence, not as a universal proof.
   262	
